      "category": "balance",
      "turn": 2,
      "user": "If I keep everything in deposits and bonds, what do I miss?",
      "status": 200,
      "content": "Mainly growth and inflation protection. Deposits and bonds pay steady, fixed returns that don't follow stock or crypto prices, so your $400,000 in Safety won't swing much. But over long periods their returns are usually lower than stocks, and if prices rise faster than they pay, your money buys a little less each year. Stocks and crypto can grow more, but they can also fall sharply, which is why the framework keeps a mix.\n\nKeeping everything in Safety is a choice you can make. Your current split is Safety $400,000 (furthest ahead of its age share), Traditional $20,000 of $163,636 with $143,636 to go, and Crypto $5,000 of $163,636 with $158,636 to go. Nothing needs to change unless you decide it does.",
